-    "- The crossing area near the centrum semiovale (right side) is smaller when including the S0 response for some reason.\n",
-    "\n",
-    "It is interesting that including the S0 response seemingly has both positive effects (better CSF segmentation) and some drawbacks (less sensitivity to crossings). It seems the S0 signal inside the crossing is slightly higher than the single bundle tissue, meaning some of the grey matter response function needs to be included in the fit (hence the green hue over the red).\n",
